WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.793
Multiplying a fraction by a whole number means several equal fractional groups; use

00:00:04.793 --> 00:00:05.853
strips to model.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:14.913
Calculate 5/8 of 48. The answer is 30. One 8th of 48 is 6; multiply by 5 to get 30.

00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:21.744
6/8 of 32 reading cards are used at a market stall. How many cards is that? Pause the

00:00:21.744 --> 00:00:22.738
video and think.

00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:29.793
6/8 of 32 reading cards are used at a market stall. How many cards is that? The

00:00:29.793 --> 00:00:35.243
answer is 24. One 8th of 32 is 4; multiply by 6 to get 24.
